// The spall cone's shape — the field thrown from every body exit a round reaches. Read by
// `src/ballistics/spall_cone.rs`, embedded and parsed once, validated at parse. The law itself
// (strength, profile, shadowing, dose) is design doc §5,
// `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`; this file holds only its shape data.
//
// Every value here is a choice the owner can change by editing this file alone; none is a
// constant of the law. The playtest fork on the half-angle and the axis is F5 in
// `.agents/scratch/playtest-forks/README.md`.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind one of Measured,
// Derived, Tuned, Resolution, Unknown (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    // Half-angle α (degrees) of the cone: the rim where the profile's strength reaches zero.
    half_angle_deg: (25.0, Tuned("provisional default, owner 2026-10-12 (playtest fork F5);
        comparable MEASURED normal-impact outer extents ~26° (Qi et al. 2026,
        .agents/scratch/damage-cam-2026-10-08/research/cloud-angle-deep.md)")),

    // The cone's axis. `RearNormalBisector`: normalize(rear-face outward normal + exit direction)
    // at a genuine exit, the exit direction at an internal step (which has no face).
    // `ExitDirection`: the exit direction everywhere.
    axis: (RearNormalBisector, Tuned("engineering assumption (playtest fork F5) with MEASURED
        support: debris axis about halfway between the shot line and the plate normal, 25°
        measured against 22.5° predicted at 45° obliquity (Verolme 1997, Recht & Howell 1967;
        research/cloud-angle-deep.md)")),

    // N, the number of directions the cone is sampled by, in equal-solid-angle strata of weight
    // 1/N. The emitted total is S/2 at every N, so N changes how finely a box's dose is resolved,
    // never how much the cone carries.
    directions: (24, Resolution("sampling of the cone; changes how finely a box's dose is
        resolved, never the emitted total")),

    // How the strength is spread over the directions. `Linear`: S·(cos θ − cos α)/(1 − cos α),
    // greatest on the axis, zero at the rim. `Flat`: S/2 along every direction, the same total.
    profile: (Linear, Tuned("design doc §5: a profile falling to zero at the rim, as the measured
        fragment fluence falls off the debris axis (research/cloud-angle-deep.md)")),

    // How a direction passes through what it meets. `Partial`: spent by chord × factor through
    // every solid, dosing each box it enters at its strength there. `FirstSolid`: stopped by the
    // first solid it enters, a box there taking its whole strength, armour none.
    passage: (Partial, Tuned("design doc §5: fragments spend their energy through what they
        cross, so a box shadows the boxes behind it")),
)
